.TH "WEBTRANSPORT.PROTOCOL" "3JS" "September 1, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
WebTransport.protocol \- WebTransport: protocol property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]protocol\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]WebTransport\f[R] interface returns the application\-specific
protocol selected by the server.
.PP
The value is selected from those offered in the \f[CR]protocols\f[R]
constructor option.
Note that the value is set once the \f[CR]ready\f[R] promise fulfills.
It is the empty string if \f[CR]protocols\f[R] was not used, or if the
server chose not to select one of the offered protocols.
.SH VALUE
A string.
Defaults to \f[CR]\(dq\(dq\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Requesting and reading a negotiated protocol
This example shows how to request a set of candidate protocols and read
back the one the server selected.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] url = \(dqhttps://example.com:4999/wt\(dq;

\f[B]async\f[R] \f[B]function\f[R] initTransport(url) {
  \f[B]const\f[R] transport = \f[B]new\f[R] WebTransport(url, {
    protocols: [\(dqchat\(dq, \(dqfile\-transfer\(dq],
  });

  \f[B]try\f[R] {
    \f[I]// The connection can be used once ready fulfills\f[R]
    \f[B]await\f[R] transport.ready;
    console.log(transport.protocol); \f[I]// e.g. \(dqchat\(dq, or \(dq\(dq if none was selected\f[R]
    \f[B]return\f[R] transport;
  } \f[B]catch\f[R] (error) {
    \f[I]// Ready may reject if the offered protocols aren\(aqt supported\f[R]
    console.error(\(gaConnection failed: ${error}\(ga);
  }
}

initTransport(url);
.EE
